I found the rule: with P = number of non-zero rows, output row i takes the color of the non-zero row j where j ≡ i (mod P). Verified on both demos.

```python
def transform(grid):
    colored = [(i, r[0]) for i, r in enumerate(grid) if any(c != 0 for c in r)]
    P = len(colored)
    if P == 0:
        return [row[:] for row in grid]
    width = len(grid[0])
    out = []
    for i in range(len(grid)):
        c = None
        for (ri, col) in colored:
            if ri % P == i % P:
                c = col
                break
        out.append([c] * width)
    return out
